
Looking at ways to make a webpage on github
all these will be static pages

1. GitHub Profile README
   - create a repo with same name as account name
     - place a README.md this will be displayed as webpage
   - You don't have to manage a domain or a complex build process
   - Most use GitHub Profile README Generators
     - example one by Aravind Binu - https://github.com/rahuldkjain/github-profile-readme-generator

2. GitHub Pages + Jekyll
   - Write your content in simple Markdown, GitHubs internal engine (Jekyll)
     turns it into professionally looking website

3. Modern Choice: Astro or Next.js + GitHub Actions
   - its faster and more modern that Jekyll. Developers build site locally
     using React or Vue and use GitHub Actions to automatically deploy the site
     to GitHub pages when they push the code
   - Many users Fork a popular portfolio template like al-folio and swap
     out the text for their own

